  "goodToKnow": "Tatverdächtig means suspected of a crime, mostly used in police and news language. Der/die Tatverdächtige (declined like an adjective) is the suspect. German media usually give only the first name and initial of suspects, like Ahmed K. or Thomas M., because of privacy rules in the press code. Die Tat is the deed, and der Tatort is the crime scene, as in the famous Sunday crime series."
